(3) KPPAD/KPPAK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) memiliki  tugas:
a. melakukan advokasi, mediasi, sosialisasi, dan fasilitasi  perlunya pemenuhan hak perempuan dan anak, serta hak  partisipasi perempuan dan anak dalam pembangunan;
b. mengumpulkan data dan informasi yang terkait  pelindungan perempuan dan anak;
c. menerima pengaduan dari masyarakat;
d. melakukan kerjasama dan koordinasi dalam melaksanakan  pemenuhan hak-hak perempuan dan anak sesuai dengan  peraturan perundang-undangan yang berlaku; dan
e. melakukan rujukan pada kasus-kasus yang tidak dapat  diselesaikan oleh KPPAD/KPPAK kepada UPTD PPA. (4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai pembentukan, tugas pokok  dan fungsi serta pengurusan KPPAD/KPPAK sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur dalam Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 30
(1) The Regional Government in an effort to provide and administer protection services for women victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination shall establish KPPAD/KPPAK.
(2) KPPAD/KPPAK as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be under and responsible to the Regional Apparatus that carries out governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection through the Village Head/Lurah with the knowledge of the local Camat.
(3) KPPAD/KPPAK as referred to in paragraph (2) shall have the duties to:
a. conduct advocacy, mediation, socialization, and facilitation of the need for fulfillment of women's and children's rights, as well as the right of women's and children's participation in development;
b. collect data and information related to the protection of women and children;
c. receive complaints from the community;
d. conduct cooperation and coordination in implementing the fulfillment of women's and children's rights in accordance with applicable laws and regulations; and
e. make referrals on cases that cannot be resolved by KPPAD/KPPAK to UPTD PPA.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment, main duties and functions as well as management of KPPAD/KPPAK as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.
